5. Termination
--------------

5.1. The rights granted under this License will terminate automatically
if You fail to comply with any of its terms. However, if You become
compliant, then the rights granted under this License from a particular
Contributor are reinstated (a) provisionally, unless and until such
Contributor explicitly or finally terminates Your grants, or (b) each
Contributor terminates Your grants by some reasonable means if You have
failed to become compliant within 30 days of receiving notice.

5.2. If You initiate litigation against any entity by claiming that the
Contributor Version infringes a patent (excluding declaratory judgment
actions, counter-claims, and cross-claims) then Your rights granted under
Section 2.1(b) from any Contributor to You for the Covered Software
shall terminate automatically as of the date such litigation is filed.

5.3. In the event of termination under Sections 5.1 or 5.2 above, all
end user license agreements (excluding distributors and resellers) which
have been validly granted by You or Your distributors under this License
prior to termination shall survive termination.

